MODULE: LivingWorldCore
TYPE: Core Infrastructure
PATH: ./Source
DESC: Single entry point for initialization, logging, and Harmony patching for all 7 submodules. Unified logging to LivingWorld.log.

FILES[1]{name, type, desc}:
LivingWorldCore.cs, Core, Centralized manager for assembly-wide Harmony registration and service startup.


MODULE: BetterGov
TYPE: Source Component
PATH: ./Source/BetterGov
DESC: Governor automation and stability system. Automates governor assignment and issue resolution while fixing native crashes.

FEATURES[4]{feature, details}:
Auto-Assign Governor, Automatically assigns party leader (of owner clan) to empty governor seat upon entering owned settlement.
Issue Resolution, Automates settlement & village issue resolution. Unified Reward Parity via reflection for player and AI clans.
Stability Layer, Patches critical native crashes (AI Visit, Diplomacy, Roster Underflow).
Configuration, Full MCM integration for toggling features and debug logging.

CONTENTS[9]{file, type, key_components}:
AutoResolveIssuesBehavior.cs, Behavior, [Class] AutoResolveIssuesBehavior : CampaignBehaviorBase, [Method] OnDailyTickSettlement (Village/Settlement Support), [Method] ResolveIssue (SolveIssue Reflection).
BetterGovSubModule.cs, Entry, [Class] BetterGovSubModule : MBSubModuleBase, [Method] OnSubModuleLoad (DI Setup), [Method] OnGameStart (Behavior Registration).
GlobalSettings.cs, Proxy, Static proxy to LivingWorldSettings.Instance.
GovernorService.cs, Service, [Class] GovernorService, [Method] HandleSettlementEntered (Auto-Assign), [Method] HandleSettlementLeft (Seat Vacation).
Patches/AiVisitSettlementCrashFix.cs, Patch, Fixes crash during AI settlement visitation.
Patches/AutoGovernorPatches.cs, Patch, [HarmonyPatch] MobileParty.CurrentSettlement(Setter) -> Hooks GovernorService.
Patches/DiplomacyCrashFix.cs, Patch, Fixes diplomacy calculation crashes.
Patches/RosterUnderflowCrashFix.cs, Patch, Prevents roster count underflow exceptions.
Patches/UniversalIssueCrashFix.cs, Patch, General catch-all for issue lifecycle checks (IssueStayAliveConditions).

CHANGELOG[2]{date, time, author, change}:
2026-01-22, 06:05, ANTIGRAVITY, Added Village Issue support and AI Reward Parity (SolveIssue Reflection).
2026-01-22, 19:40, ANTIGRAVITY, Code Cleanup: Removed hardcoded drive paths and panic logging.
2026-01-21, 22:15, USER, Detailed structure update with feature/call mapping.


PROJECT: FieldSquire
TYPE: Module
PATH: Source/FieldSquire
DESC: Autonomous Squire system. Focuses on party logistics, automated supply management, and dynamic interactions via a hidden, non-combatant utility companion.

FILES[12]{name, type, note}
LivingWorldCore.cs, Root, Consolidated entry point for the assembly.
FieldSquireSubModule.cs, Submodule, Registers behaviors and participates in startup sequence.
GlobalSettings.cs, Proxy, Static proxy to LivingWorldSettings.Instance.
SquireSpawnBehavior.cs, Behavior, Manages creation/existence of the "field_squire" entity.
SquireDialogBehavior.cs, Behavior, Handles conversation flows (Supplies, Ledger, Headhunting).
SquireLogisticsBehavior.cs, Behavior, Automates food purchasing (maintains threshold).
SquireUIPatches.cs, Patch, Manual Harmony patches: Hides Squire from Inventory, CharSheet, Governor, and Party selection.
PartySizeLimitPatch.cs, Patch, Adds +1 Party Size to offset Squire taking a slot.
SquireCombatPatch.cs, Patch, Prevents Squire from spawning in combat missions.
SquireImmortalityPatch.cs, Patch, Intercepts KillCharacterAction to prevent death.
SquireWageAndFoodPatch.cs, Patch, Sets Squire wage to 0. (Name is valid, logic is Wage only).
SquireXpBlockPatch.cs, Patch, Prevents Squire from gaining any XP.
SquireTownManagementVM.cs, ViewModel, Remote access to TownManagementVM via reflection.

CALLS[6]{target, hook}
KillCharacterAction.ApplyInternal, Prefix (Immortality Intercept)
Mission.SpawnTroop, Prefix (Combat Block)
DefaultPartyWageModel.GetCharacterWage, Prefix (Wage = 0)
Hero.AddSkillXp, Prefix (Block XP Gain)
SPInventoryVM.CanSelectHero, Postfix (Hide from Inventory UI)
CharacterDeveloperVM.GetApplicableHeroes, Postfix (Hide from Character Sheet)

FEATURES[6]{name, status, note}
Autonomous Resupply, ACTIVE, Logic in LogisticsBehavior.
Combat Protection, ACTIVE, Patched out of battle spawns.
Immortality, ACTIVE, Heal(1) intervention on death event.
Dialog System, ACTIVE, Service-based flows + Remote Town Management.
Wanderer Search, ACTIVE, Headhunting feature in DialogBehavior.
UI Hiding, ACTIVE, Squire hidden from Inventory, CharSheet, Governor, and Party leader selection.

CHANGELOG[7]{date, time, desc, status}
2026-01-22, 12:00, Fixed SquireDialogBehavior search loop to return to menu, COMPLETED
2026-01-22, 12:20, Implemented SquireInventoryPatch to hide focus-character from inventory, COMPLETED
2026-01-22, 21:15, Refactor SquireDialogBehavior for dynamic conversation flow (Fixed Menu-Return), COMPLETED
2026-01-24, 09:00, Consolidated all FieldSquire UI patches into SquireUIPatches.cs, COMPLETED
2026-01-29, 01:50, Consolidated LivingWorld assembly into LivingWorldCore hub, COMPLETED
2026-01-29, 02:20, Removed unsuccessful Issue blocking patches after build performance assessment, COMPLETED


METADATA:
WORKSPACE, LivingWorld
MODULE, HappyParty
PATH, Source/HappyParty
LAST_UPDATE, 2026-01-21
TYPE, Logic/Behaviors
DESCRIPTION, AI Life Improvement System. Enhances AI Lord capability (recruitment, food variety, role assignment) and manages world population (Wanderer spawning, cleanup of stuck heroes).

FILES[9]{name, type, size, desc}:
CustomWandererSpawnBehavior.cs, Behavior, 6KB, Maintains minimal Wanderer population via daily spawns.
EliteRecruiterBehavior.cs, Behavior, 4KB, AI Lords recruit Tier 3+ troops from notables.
GlobalSettings.cs, Proxy, 2KB, Static proxy to LivingWorldSettings.Instance.
GourmetArmyBehavior.cs, Behavior, 4KB, AI Lords buy diverse food for morale.
HappyPartySubModule.cs, Module, 5KB, Entry point. Registers ButterLib services/loggers.
JobSeekerBehavior.cs, Behavior, 7KB, AI hires Wanderers. Adds Prisoner Dialogue (Release/Exec) for ALL captured Wanderers.
RansomPrisonerBehavior.cs, Behavior, 4KB, AI Lords ransom prisoners and recruit high-tier captives.
TavernCleanerBehavior.cs, Behavior, 4KB, Daily cleanup of stuck heroes in settlements. Fixes Ghost Prisoners.
TavernShooBehavior.cs, Behavior, 5KB, Dialogue to force-move heroes. Contains core 'Shoo' logic.

FEATURES[6]{id, name, logic}:
SPAWN.01, Infinite Wanderers, Checks GlobalSettings.TargetWandererCount daily. Spawns templates at random towns if below cap.
AI.01, Elite Recruitment, AI Lords scan notable volunteer lists on settlement enter. Buy Tier 3+ troops if wealthy.
AI.02, Gourmet Diet, AI Lords purchase low-stock food items to maximize morale variety. Removes stock from settlement to preserve economy.
AI.03, Headhunting, AI Lords with low skills (Medicine/Eng/Scout/Stew) hire high-skill Wanderers from taverns.
AI.04, Auto Ransom, AI Lords ransom prisoners for gold and recruit Tier 4+ prisoners if party has space.
CLEANUP.01, Tavern Shoo, periodically forces stuck/party-less nobles & wanderers to join clan parties or form new ones. Includes 'Ghost Prisoner' fix.

CALLS[7]{source, event, target}:
HappyPartySubModule, OnSubModuleLoad, ButterLib.AddSerilogLoggerProvider
HappyPartySubModule, OnGameStart, CampaignGameStarter.AddBehavior (DI-based)
CustomWandererSpawnBehavior, OnDailyTick, SpawnMissingWanderers
EliteRecruiterBehavior, OnSettlementEntered, Recruit from notables
JobSeekerBehavior, OnSettlementEntered, CheckAndHire (Surgeon, Engineer, Scout, Quartermaster)
TavernCleanerBehavior, OnDailyTick, ExecuteShoo (batch), FixGhostPrisoners
TavernShooBehavior, OnSessionLaunched, AddDialogs ("happyparty_shoo_ask")

CHANGELOG[5]{date, time, version, notes}:
2026-01-21, 22:15, v1.0.1, Enhanced summary with full feature/call analysis.
2026-01-21, 22:30, v1.0.2, Code Cleanup: Removed legacy comments, fix typos, optimized Shoo logic (suppress spam).
2026-01-22, 13:35, v1.0.3, Fixed TavernShoo teleportation bug causing KeyNotFound crash.
2026-01-23, 22:45, v1.0.4, Added Universal Wanderer Prisoner Dialogue (Execute/Release) to bypass native lockout.
2026-01-26, 22:15, v1.0.5, Added SettlementClaimantDecisionPatch to exclude Wanderers from Kingdom Decisions.
2026-01-26, 22:15, v1.0.5, Added SettlementClaimantDecisionPatch to exclude Wanderers from Kingdom Decisions.
2026-01-26, 22:45, v1.0.6, Removed Wanderer Party creation from TavernShooBehavior (Root Cause Fix).
2026-01-26, 22:55, v1.0.7, REVERTED v1.0.6 (Restored Shoo Parties). Added TavernCleaner.FixStuckCompanions to fire AI-hired wanderers stuck in limbo.
2026-01-26, 23:05, v1.0.8, Refined Shoo Logic: If no clan party found, AI Wanderers are FIRED (neutralized) instead of creating new parties.
2026-01-26, 23:15, v1.0.9, Moved TavernCleaner.FixStuckCompanions to OnSessionLaunched for immediate cleanup on load.
2026-01-26, 23:30, v1.1.0, Added FixBuggedWandererParties to disband existing invalid wanderer parties on load. Implemented Reflection-based ForceRemoveFromClan for robust cleanup.
FUTURE, TBD, v1.1.0, Planned feature expansion.
FUTURE, TBD, v1.2.0, Performance optimization.
FUTURE, TBD, v1.3.0, Refactoring behaviors.


@context HonestWork Module Summary
@format TOON 1.4
@generated_at 2026-01-22
@target_directory e:\Bannerlord_Mods\Modules\LivingWorld\Source\HonestWork

FILES[8]{name, desc, key_calls}:
CastleJobBehavior.cs, Castle employment & Garrison drilling, ProcessAIHourlyWork; ApplyCastleShiftRewards; GiveHourlyReward
GlobalSettings.cs, Proxy, Static proxy to LivingWorldSettings.Instance.
HonestWorkHelpers.cs, Shared arithmetic & party utilities, GiveRandomPartyXp; GetPartyTotalTier
HonestWorkSubModule.cs, Bootstrapper & Serilog setup, OnSubModuleLoad; OnGameStart; AddSerilogLoggerProvider
NavalIntegration.cs, Soft dependency layer for NavalDLC, IsEnabled; Mariner; HasShipyard; Initialize
TownJobBehavior.cs, 10 Town Jobs (7 Base + 3 Naval); Crime; Tavern Cleaning, InitializeJobs; ProcessAIHourlyWork; CheckForArrest; CleanTavern
VillageLaborBehavior.cs, Village Labor & Noble Recruitment, ProcessAIHourlyWork; AccelerateRecruitSpawning; CheckAndRecruitEliteTroops
Patches/JobImpactPatches.cs, Harmony Patch, UI Tooltip Integration. Injects job impacts into Settlement Models (Loyalty/Security/Prosperity/Militia/Food).

FEATURES[7]{category, details}:
TownJobs, 10 Types: Guard(Sec), Thug(Crime), Artisan(Prosp), Official(Food), Physician(Loyalty), Instructor(XP), Outrider(Patrol) + 3 Naval (DLC)
NavalDLC Integration, Soft dependency for Deckhand, Shipwright, Harbormaster. Docks-sensitive filtering via 'NavalIntegration'
WorkCycle, Hourly Tick for Wage/XP -> 4-Hour Shift for Bonus Rewards. Jobs hidden while Player is in an Army.
CriminalSystem, Thug jobs risk arrest based on Town Security vs Roguery. Implements 'StartCrimeCooldown' for AI.
SeasonalEconomy, Wages fluctuate based on Campaign Season (Winter/Summer) via 'UpdateSeasonalMultipliers'
CompanionAssist, Non-wounded party members contribute skill bonuses to Player's job efficiency (Leadership/Trade/etc)
NobleFarming, AI Lords patrol villages to recruit Elite Troops (Tier 2+) to fill party slots via 'CheckAndRecruitEliteTroops'
UiIntergration, Tooltips display "Player Job" and "Town Jobs" impacts on Settlement stats. Visualizes Food/Militia/Prosperity changes.


CHANGELOG[3]{date, time, change}:
2026-01-22, 06:25, Restricted job visibility to exclude situations where Player is in an Army (Town/Village/Castle)
2026-01-22, 07:00, Integrated 3 Naval DLC Dependent Jobs with reflection-based soft dependency layer (Deckhand/Shipwright/Harbormaster)
2026-01-23, 03:55, Fixed crash in GiveRandomPartyXp caused by invalid XP range (Min > Max)
2026-01-23, 23:20, UI Integration: Added Harmony patches to display job effects in Town Management tooltips. Refactored TownJobBehavior to prevent stat double-dipping.


MODULE: Landlord
DESC: Economic/finance model & behavior logic for land ownership system.
PATH: Source/Landlord

FILES[7]{name, type, desc}:
EconomyBehavior.cs, Behavior, Core logic for buying/managing land & production cycles.
GlobalSettings.cs, Proxy, Static proxy to LivingWorldSettings.Instance.
LandlordFinanceModel.cs, Model, Integrates estate income into Clan Finance logic.
ViolenceBehavior.cs, Behavior, Handles raiding, razing, and plot defense during map events.
LandlordState.cs, State, Defines VillagePlot and LandlordManager data structures.
LandlordSubModule.cs, Entry, Registration of behaviors, models, and logging.
VillageWealthBehavior.cs, Behavior, Manages village wealth stimulus and militia patrols.

FEATURES[7]{name, detail}:
Plot Ownership, Buy up to 3 plots per village (Normal/Good/Great tiers).
Production, Choose from 7 categories (Food, Livestock, Goods, etc) with efficiency logic.
Management, Upgrade Guardhouses (Garrison/Stash), toggle Gold/Item yield split.
AI Economy, AI Lords dynamically purchase land based on wealth and random crop selection.
Warfare, Raze enemy plots for loot; plot garrisons join village militia in defense.
Caravan Inquiries, Player caravans notify owner of available land during trade stops.
Village Stimulus, Payouts inject gold into villages (deficit coverage + 50% stimulus).

UI_FEEDBACK[2]{trigger, format, detail}:
Daily Report (H22), [Landlord] Daily Report: Earned {X}g from {Y} estates., Aggregated wealth summary in gold color.
Action Alerts, InformationMessage / Inquiry, Immediate feedback for purchases, upgrades, and raiding.

MECHANICS[3]{system, factor, effect}:
Efficiency, Season/Culture/Hearths, Dynamic yield scaling (factors from -0.2 to +0.3).
Hearth Growth, Plot Tier, Daily village growth bonus (+0.1 to +0.5 hearths).
Bonus Products, Animal Crops, Automatic generation of Butter/Cheese (Cows) or Wool (Sheep).

CALLS[4]{target, method, note}:
EconomyBehavior, GetItemsByCategory, Filters items for production menus.
LandlordManager, GlobalPlots, Main data store for all village plots.
LandlordFinanceModel, CalculateClanIncome, Injects daily income into clan budget.
ViolenceBehavior, ModifyHearths, Adjusts village hearths on raze/raid.

CHANGELOG[4]{date, time, desc, status}:
