MODULE: LivingLegend
TYPE: SubModule/Component
DESC: Late-game fame mechanics allowing Renown to be spent as a currency for power, patrols, and forced recruitment.
STATUS: ACTIVE

FILES[8]{name, desc}:
GlobalSettings.cs, Proxy, Static proxy to LivingWorldSettings.Instance.
LivingLegendBehavior.cs, Core logic: DailyTick (Decay/AI), Dialogs (CallToArms/Recruit), Menus (Rally).
LivingLegendModel.cs, Game Models: +Companion Limit, +Militia/Loyalty (Legend's Aura).
LivingLegendPatches.cs, Harmony: ArmyManagementVM (Shift-Click to pay Renown for army).
LivingLegendSubModule.cs, Init: Logger, Harmony, DI Registration.
MilitiaPatrolComponent.cs, Custom PartyComponent for rallied militia.
LivingLegendTypeDefiner.cs, Output of SaveSystem processing (likely).


FEATURES[5]{id, trigger, effect}:
LEGEND_AURA, Passive (Daily), Bonus Loyalty/Militia & +Companion Slots if Renown > Threshold. Daily Renown Decay.
RALLY_MILITIA, Village Menu, Spend Renown to spawn a 40-man Militia Patrol for 5 days. (AI Supported).
CALL_TO_ARMS, Lord Dialog, Spend Renown (500) to force a lord into your army instantly.
RENOWN_RECRUIT, Army Mgmt (Shift+Done), Spend Renown instead of Influence to recruit parties to army.
MINOR_RECRUIT, Minor Leader Dialog, Spend Renown (2000) to recruit Minor Faction leader as companion.

CALLS[3]{type, target, note}:
EVENT, CampaignEvents.DailyTickClanEvent, Handles Renown Decay and AI Militia spawning.
PATCH, ArmyManagementVM.ExecuteDone, Intercepts 'Done' to allow Renown payment via Shift key.
MENU, village (Rally Militia), Adds 'Rally the Peasantry' option to villages.

CHANGELOG[3]{date, time, change}:
2026-01-22, 04:12, Scanned code. Documented features: Legend Aura, Militia Rally, Renown Recruitment.
FUTURE, TBD, Implement fame decay system (Dynamic decay based on inactivity?).
FUTURE, TBD, Add bard reputation mechanics.


META:
TYPE: Summary
TARGET: e:\Bannerlord_Mods\Modules\LivingWorld\Source\NewClans
GENERATED: 2026-01-21T22:35:10-06:00
CONTEXT: NewClans Source Code

FILES[4]{name, desc}:
GlobalSettings.cs, Proxy, Static proxy to LivingWorldSettings.Instance.
NewClansBehavior.cs, Core logic for Companion->Noble promotion (Player & AI). Handles settlement transfer/theft.
NewClansSubModule.cs, Initializes Harmony patches & registers CampaignBehavior.
Patches/BanditSpawnCrashPatch.cs, Harmony Prefix on BanditSpawnCampaignBehavior.IsBanditFaction to prevent KeyNotFound crash for custom bandits.

SETTINGS[3]{key, default, desc}:
ModuleEnabled, true, Master toggle for behavior injection.
PromotionCost, 1000000, Denars required to promote a companion.
DebugMode, false, Enables verbose logging to file.

FEATURES[4]{category, detail}:
Player Logic, Dialogue option to promote companion. Costs gold. Auto-seizes fief from 'Greedy' clans (T5+, >1 Fiefs) or Player's own.
AI Logic, Weekly tick checks wealthy clans (T5+, >2M Gold, >3 Fiefs). 10% weekly chance to promote wanderer to new vassal clan using own castle.
Stability, 'Ghost Clan' prevention logic: Forces settlement ownership transfer if CreateCompanionToLordClan fails assignments.
Crash Fix, Whitelists vanilla bandit factions (Looters/Mountain/Forest/Sea/Steppe/Desert) to bypass native Hideout dictionary crash.

